{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RemoteChange","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every field describes the whole burst, not its last notification. A burst is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one window as far as the merge is concerned, and “the last one wins” would"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"silently drop every notification but one — on a debounce that exists"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"precisely because bursts are expected, that is a change quietly going"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"missing rather than a visible failure."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Only notifications the observer "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"accepted"}]},{"type":"text","text":" are represented. A notification"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from a store the observer was told it doesn’t own is dropped before it gets"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"here; one whose store can’t be identified is always accepted, and sets"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/documentation\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/RemoteChange\/includesUnidentifiedStore"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Why-there-is-no-history-token","type":"heading","text":"Why there is no history token"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The underlying notification carries ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPersistentHistoryTokenKey"},{"type":"text","text":", and it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deliberately not surfaced. That value is a CoreData "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPersistentHistoryToken"},{"type":"text","text":";"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the watermark in "},{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a SwiftData "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DefaultHistoryToken"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whose only public initializer is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(from:)"},{"text":" — there is no supported","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conversion between the two, and SwiftData’s interface names no CoreData type","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"at all. Publishing a token that neither Swidux nor an app author can act on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"would be an invitation to misuse it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Nothing is lost by leaving it out: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistenceCoordinator.mergeChanges(into:policy:)"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"anchors its watermark on the highest token in the window it just scanned, so","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the token it needs is one it already holds."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxcloudkitsync\/remotechange"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The stores one coalesced burst of remote-change notifications named.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/documentation\/SwiduxCloudKitSync"]]},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/documentation\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/RemoteChange\/init(storeURLs:storeUUIDs:includesUnidentifiedStore:notificationCount:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Initializers"},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/documentation\/SwiduxCloudKitSync\/RemoteChange\/includesUnidentifie